union task_kind =
    | Epic :: task_kind
    | Feature :: task_kind
    | Story :: task_kind
    | TaskKind :: task_kind

union priority =
    | P0 :: priority | P1 :: priority | P2 :: priority | P3 :: priority | P4 :: priority | P5 :: priority

union difficulty =
    | D0 :: difficulty | D1 :: difficulty | D2 :: difficulty | D3 :: difficulty | D4 :: difficulty
    | D5 :: difficulty | D6 :: difficulty | D7 :: difficulty | D8 :: difficulty

union task_status =
    | Planned :: task_status | Active :: task_status | Blocked :: task_status | Paused :: task_status | Done :: task_status

union agile_item =
    | Task :: string * string * task_kind * priority * difficulty * u32 * task_status * string * string * string * string -> agile_item

inl eoie_dogfood () = Task ("EOIE-DOGFOOD", "Use eoie for our agile backlog and tool runs with the compiler configured, and fix every friction so it beats Claude Code tools: (1) unbounded/renewing lease on local machines, configurable, no per-lease reports (user); (2) help and inspection never blocked by an expired lease, accept --help on every verb; (3) agile list renders a table (id, P, D, %, status, title) instead of raw .spi lines; (4) agile status shows local times and remaining minutes instead of unix ms; (5) agile add to create tasks; (6) agile init scaffolds a root (state/, package.spiproj with agile+prompt); (7) actionable package-graph errors (|core- in state package was rejected without a reason); (8) record-preflight must not demand eoie release files (history, ratings, bench, migration) from a plain backlog root; done 2026-10-08: (1) EOIE_LEASE_POLICY=renewing, (5) agile add, (9) agile edit, (3) in progress; acceptance bar: every verb beats its pwsh counterpart: elapsed time, counts, bytes, exit code, stderr digest, cache hits in every result; aligned human output plus --json; diagnostics that run the obvious intent instead of only suggesting it; findings (9) agile edit for descriptions/notes; (10) eoie help <capability> should show proxy help instead of exit 2; (11) normalize path separators in outputs (root\\\\.github/x); (12) say expected vs received argument count on bad arguments; (13) dev.ps1 should accept module names (agile_state_runtime_policy_domain) as well as package names; (14) a failed cargo check must surface the first rustc error, not only 'Cargo rejected regenerated EOIE owners'; (15) fs-search must accept '.' as the root itself; 08:2x done: (3) agile list table sorted by priority with status counts and elapsed_ms, (9) agile edit; new findings (16) text-replace needs --all/--expect N for multi-match edits; (17) EOIE_LEASE_POLICY should also come from the eoie config file (shells started before the user env var miss it); (18) fs-remove prints nothing on success; (19) list header % column off by one; (20) inspection (text-replace check) still lease-blocked; 08:4x done: (4) agile status shows phase, policy and relative times (started=2h49m_ago) beside the raw unix fields, (17) lease policy from <config>/eoie/lease-policy (this machine: renewing) with EOIE_LEASE_POLICY still first, (19) list header aligned, (20) text-replace check / *-preview modes are inspections (effect key verb:sub:mode, lookup moved from rust_global into Spiral crate agile_lease_terms); contract tests isolate EOIE_LEASE_POLICY and EOIE_CONFIG_HOME; 08:5x done: (2)+(10) --help/-h anywhere after a verb or subcommand and help <capability> answer with exit 0 before the lease guard (Spiral help_request union in command_spec_domain); left: (6) agile init, (7) package-graph errors, (8) record-preflight, (11) path separators, (12) arg-count diagnostics, (13) dev.ps1 module names, (14) cargo error surfacing, (15) fs-search ., (16) text-replace --all, (18) fs-remove receipt, enriched outputs everywhere; 08:5x done: (6) agile init <root> scaffolds state/package.spiproj + the typed agile.spi schema (Spiral crate agile_backlog_scaffold, Renew effect like begin); init -> begin -> add -> check verified on a fresh root; 09:1x done: (12) agile arity errors name the expected shape and received operand count, (16) text-replace migrated from the legacy rust_global arm to Spiral crate proxy_text_replacement: --expect N / --all, typed mode/expectation unions, rooted path via rust_std_fs (finding 11 for this verb), atomic replace + readback, receipt with matches/expected/bytes/elapsed_ms; 09:2x done: (18) fs-remove migrated to Spiral crate proxy_file_removal with a receipt (path, kind file|symlink, bytes, elapsed_ms) and typed rejections (missing, directory -> use fs-remove-tree, root escape), (15) fs-search <root> . searches the root (Spiral search_scope union; . stays rejected for mutating verbs so fs-remove-tree . cannot wipe a root); left: (7) package-graph errors, (8) record-preflight, (13) dev.ps1 module names, (14) cargo error surfacing, enriched receipts on the remaining legacy verbs; 09:4x done: (13) dev.ps1 accepts crate directory names and underscored names (resolved to Cargo package names, unknown names still rejected), (14) a failed cargo check now puts the first rustc error block into the thrown message; left: (7) package-graph errors, (8) record-preflight wording for plain backlogs, enriched receipts on the remaining legacy verbs; 09:5x done: proxy run/command failures are no longer reported as usage errors: a child that exits N makes eoie exit N with a plain error after its receipt (Spiral crate proxy_failure_classification: ArgumentFailure | ChildProcessFailure), misuse still exits 2 with usage; evidence renewed ready=True at 09:41 (before this change: renew again at end of day); 10:1x done: agile list <root> [filter] --json emits one JSON document {tasks[], shown, filter, counts{planned,active,blocked,paused,done}, elapsed_ms} (listing_format union; status census split into Spiral crate agile_task_census and scan helpers moved into agile_task_text to stay under the 1000-line crate gate); quotes and backslashes round-trip; raw tabs in titles are not escaped yet (spi_escaped lacks \\t); 10:5x done: (7) the compiler host now says which packages failed and why a |core- packages: entry fails (SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR or a deps/The-Spiral-Language clone); verified: with the variable set the same backlog checks clean (spiral dev24); 10:4x done: (8) agile check prints \"records catalog=v1 present=0/4 missing=... (agile check does not need them)\" from the new typed crate agile_record_catalog (RecordCatalogComplete | RecordCatalogPartial), replacing the ready=0 text in the rust_global blob; spi_escaped escapes tabs; eoie_agile_state.spi unchanged vs HEAD; 195/195; 11:0x receipts: fs-copy migrated whole into typed crate proxy_file_copy (elapsed_ms, precise rooted errors kept); agile set receipt from typed crate agile_update_receipt (bytes_before/after + elapsed_ms like agile edit); parallel-search accepts . as the whole root; workspace_primitives.rooted shares proxy argument + root confinement (fs-remove/text-replace regenerated byte-identical); 195/195. Next: parallel-search receipt elapsed, hit-limit truncation instead of abort (needs inspection_collect migrated out of rust_global); 12:5x parallel-search: new typed receipt crate proxy_search_receipt shows serial_ms/parallel_ms/elapsed_ms; it exposed a 111 s search of eoie/src (src/target = 61,538 files, 11.7 GB of build output); the search walk now skips build output (typed search_directory: .git, node_modules, CACHEDIR.TAG or .rustc_info.json) and the receipt says excludes=...: 1.5 s, same 7 hits; hash-tree/manifest walks unchanged; 195/195; 13:1x parallel-search over max-hits truncates deterministically instead of aborting (each subtree keeps limit+1, serial/parallel parity holds) and the typed receipt says hits=N truncated=true found_at_least=N+1 (hit_budget union); fs-search, which has no receipt, keeps an explicit error naming EOIE_SEARCH_MAX_HITS; 195/195; 16:37 evidence renewed after the afternoon batch (chain.ps1 -SkipBuild, label r1008b): cold renewal 119/119 chains, agile check --compiler exit 0, closeout applied, strict preflight -RequireReady ready=True diagnostics=0 (the pre-closeout gates rejected the stale Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock receipts the new crates changed, as expected); 17:0x new verb proxy command-output <root> <timeout-ms> <program> [args...]: prints the child stdout/stderr directly, then a typed receipt (crate proxy_command_output: ok|child-failed status elapsed_ms stdout_bytes stderr_bytes) and propagates the child exit code; replaces the command-capture + read-receipt two-step for git reads; registered in usage/help/lease (nested eoie child at index 4) and legacy surface; lesson: proxy_direct_route_names is positional (route code = index), legacy-dispatched verbs stay out of it; 195/195; 17:04 evidence renewed again after command-output (label r1008d): cold renewal, agile check --compiler exit 0, strict preflight ready=True diagnostics=0; 17:4x parallel-search aborted on the first symlink child (refusing symlink: dice\\deps\\polyglot), so whole-repo searches of dice/polyglot failed; symlink children are now a typed SymlinkEntry (not descended, receipt excludes=...,symlinks) while a symlinked start path still errors; dice searches 0.2 s; 195/195; eoie changed again, evidence renewal due; 18:16 evidence renewed after the symlink fix: strict preflight ready=True diagnostics=0", Epic, P0, D6, 94u32, Active, "", "eoie,dogfood,agile", "current", "current")
inl readable_generated_names () = Task ("READABLE-GENERATED-NAMES", "Generated code as human readable as possible on every backend: functions, unions, union cases, layouts and closures named after their Spiral source (join point, method and type names) instead of method12, U3, closure7; the numeric index only on name collisions or where inlining and join points leave no name; local names inside bodies derived from the Spiral bindings where possible. Performance first: naming must not change codegen shape or runtime cost; oracle outputs keep agreeing while residual hashes change once; build the naming as an onion layer (our own naming pass the backends consult) so upstream codegen diffs stay small; 2026-10-08 investigation: names already exist: LangEnv.join_point_method_key_names / join_point_closure_key_names map each join point key to its Spiral name (used for EJP diagnostics) but PartEvalResult does not expose them; 34 naming sites (method{tag}/closure{tag}) across ~12 backends, C/F#/Python/Cuda are upstream sections; plan: expose the tables in PartEvalResult (both cores), one GeneratedNames section maps tag -> sanitized source name (+ suffix on collision, deterministic in tag order), backends call it; upstream sections need a one-call hook each (decide with the upstream onion move); then one reviewed re-bless; 2026-10-08 14:2x correction: the names already flow: single-flight stores jp_name in each join_point_method entry, hopac in JpMethodBodyCellReadyPayload, and C/Cpp (upstream) already emit them (loop, score, derivative...; anonymous join points stay method{n}); the other backends dropped them with | body, range, _ ->; slice 1: generatedMethodName (CodegenRust section: [A-Za-z0-9_] sanitized, {name}_{tag} so it cannot meet v{n}/closure{n}/US0_ names; Gleam lowercased) used by Rust, Delphi, Zig, Lean, Bend, Gleam, Lua, TypeScript, Python through a per-codegen tag->name map; dev review: 2,018 jobs, no regression, DISAGREE 0, 286 changed rows proven identical after name normalization, the rest Bend prelude/helper names derived from method names; F# left: CodegenFsharp precedes generatedMethodName and codegenMethodBody (move the helper earlier), and hopac F# drops methodName at the cell classification (167864/167872, CodegenJpMethodBodyCellReady has no name; its codegen uses concurrent collections); 15:2x blessed (dev28 deployed): 2,018 rows, review = bless run row for row, 338 changed rows all renames (fn method0 -> fn fib_0; stems seen: loop, score, derivative, make_star, regex_compare, canonical_derivative); F# in both cores implemented (helper moved to the end of CodegenUtils; hopac carries (range, sourceName) through the generic cell unions), build + review next; 16:0x F# blessed (dev29): 41 rows changed, 39 proven rename-only vs HEAD (2 format_any carry the blessed renumbering), renamed .fsx run in dotnet fsi exit 0 (the harness only compiles F#); now every backend names functions after the Spiral source (C/Cpp {name}{tag}, the rest {name}_{tag}); upstream export: CodegenC/CodegenFsharp/CodegenUtils clean, CodegenPython 2 conflicts (section already differs from the fork there); next slices: closures (closure{n}) and union/layout names; closures next: single-flight stores names only for methods (165470); closure entries are (domain_args, body), hopac keeps closure names only in join_point_closure_key_names (diagnostics); closure naming needs PartEval to store a name in the closure entry (upstream section) before any backend can use it; 18:0x found by the dice regression build: join points named after operators (e.g. |>) sanitized to underscore-only names (fn ___9, def ___3); generatedMethodName now falls back to method{tag} unless the source name has a letter or digit; suite review all parity (no sample has operator-named join points), deployed dev30 (both cores), dice outputs regenerated", Epic, P1, D6, 65u32, Active, "", "compiler,codegen,readability", "current", "current")
