inl bend_backend () = Task ("BEND-BACKEND", "Bend 2 backend named Bend, Windows-native toolchain (bun from source), as stable as Zig/Lean/Rust/C: IO codegen, unions, tuples, arrays, strings, closures, 8/16-bit ints, harness list; 2026-10-08 09:3x: 115/133 agree (was 72), 0 wrong: mutable aliased arrays as a one-slot Chan cell holding a power-of-two Bend Array (per-element-type helper set, O(log n) peek/swap, bounds abort 3), nested arrays, unions holding arrays/functions declared is Type, closures as lambdas over closure defs; harness Bend list 116 + Known bounds row; left: floats (Bend 2 has F32 only, no formatter), i64/u8, 2 raw-macro while samples, 1 macro sample; 10:1x blessed: review run and bless run identical on 2004 rows (6 FOR-D rows filtered by design), oracle now holds the 116 Bend rows; 10:2x: F32 (Bend F32 ops/compare, decimal literals with F32.neg/division for negatives, inf, nan, signed i32<->f32 helpers) -> 119/133 agree; deployed dev23; harness Bend list 120; left: f64 (no Bend F64; emulating it in F32 would change results), i64/u8, 2 mutable-layout samples, 2 raw-macro while samples, 1 raw-macro sample; 10:4x blessed C+Bend (350 rows; review and bless runs identical; the 116 earlier Bend residuals changed only by the 23-line F32 prelude); oracle holds 120 Bend rows; 13:2x coverage probe (test.ps1 -Suite examples -Native -Probe Bend, 229 Bend rows, outputs in the scratch dir): 119 agree (exactly the listed set) + 1 known, DISAGREE 0; the 108 others: 33 raw C macros/ABI, 16 negative samples rejected everywhere, 23 BackendSwitch records without a Bend key (while_* and native_cube_* assign through !!!!BackendSwitch: needs mutable locals; Rust/Python-specific samples; lib functions without Bend arms), f64 x5 (Bend 2 has only Nat/U32/F32: no faithful f64), u64 x2 (native_closure_union_rec, rust_static_closure_chain: Nat mod 2^64), the integer zoo ts_int_wrap (u8/i8 via U32 masking), layouts x4 (heap/mut records); next by unlock size: mutable locals for while/assignment, then u64 via Nat, then small ints; 17:5x u64 decision input: Bend 2 Nat is unary (type Nat: Zero | Succ, Nat.add/sub recurse per unit), so u64 via Nat is not viable; it needs a (U32, U32) two-word encoding with carry add/sub/mul and 64/32 long division, for 2 unlockable samples: parked", Feature, P1, D7, 92u32, Active, "", "backend,bend", "current", "current")
inl compiler_upstream_onion () = Task ("COMPILER-UPSTREAM-ONION", "Move the compiler into the upstream fork's repo with our changes as onion layers over mrakgr's files (PR-ready), one file per backend, splitter adapted for parallel builds; 2026-10-08 first upstream-ready patch: CodegenC (user globals reach C output; (void)x in empty decref bodies, 211 -Wunused-parameter -> 0 apart from one stale output), made line-local so scripts/upstream.py exports it cleanly (4 hunks): python scripts/upstream.py export deps/The-Spiral-Language HEAD <out> --since HEAD writes The Spiral Language 2/CodegenC.fs; opening the PR on the fork is the user's call; 18:2x readable-names + C patch material now durable at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\upstream-pr\\names-and-c (CodegenC, CodegenFsharp, CodegenPython, CodegenUtils); both CodegenPython conflicts resolved by intent (fork already carries the string option source name in join_point_method); upstream.py export fix: an addition after the last line of a section goes to the end of the target file (it was spliced between codegen_env and its members); generatedMethodName uses System.Char (CodegenUtils opens only System.Text); verified by a differential build of the fork (unpatched vs patched, external includes restored from history): 0 patch-only errors, with a canary type error proving fsc reaches the codegen files past the unrelated lib/fsharp/Common.fs errors; 21:1x CodegenC now emits the backend standard includes before user globals (Seq.append globals env.globals |> Seq.distinct): user globals using bool/size_t no longer precede <stdbool.h>; dev review: only the include order changed in the 2 samples with C globals (Lean exit=-1 rows were load kills, parity alone); deployed dev32 both cores; patch material CodegenC.fs refreshed (export --since 98492a63, since the 18:34 commit moved HEAD past the names work)", Epic, P1, D8, 10u32, Planned, "", "compiler,upstream", "current", "current")
inl hopac_speed () = Task ("HOPAC-SPEED", "Measure hopac vs single-flight (real-work rows 3-22x slower, fresh process per job), split startup from evaluation, profile and iterate to single-flight speed; stats 2026-10-08 09:5x (probe.ps1, fresh process per compile, F# backend, mean of runs 2-3, net = total - frontier_hello baseline): startup sf 1.0s / hopac 1.45s; net eval brzozowski 0.65s / 0.8s (1.2x), zeta 0.95 / 1.4 (1.5x), omniledger 2.65 / 5.0 (1.9x), lean_cic 1.8 / 5.5 (3.1x), spiral_proves 1.5 / 4.65 (3.1x); the suite-level 126x median compares warm single-flight workers with fresh hopac processes and overstates the gap; next: profile lean_cic; profile lean_cic hopac (probe -Profile 12, SPIRAL_DIAG_QUIET=1), innermost compiler frames: term 36%, installBridge 7.4% (thread-local tail-result bridge save/restore per declared JP step), ty_core_impl 6.8%, buildFreshApplyState 3.2%, DiagSidecar.emitReentryKeySample 2.6% (runs even when quiet: ConditionalWeakTable + 2 AddOrUpdate per re-entry; counts may feed hot-key fallback, check before gating), DiagJson runner/loop/emitRecord 5.5% (background thread, CPU not wall), EvalWorklist replay tick 2.3%; candidates: gate sidecar sampling when quiet if counts are diagnostic-only, make the bridge scope a struct/stack instead of ThreadLocal round trips; each change needs an A/B probe on lean_cic/spiral_proves; 11:3x A/B (tmp/hopac-speed/ab-threadlocal.ps1, 2 interleaved rounds, runs 2-3): the 4 hot-path JP slots AsyncLocal -> ThreadLocal gave identical outputs on 4 samples but lean_cic 6.15/6.50 -> 6.15/6.20 s, spiral_proves 6.10/6.15 -> 5.95/6.10 s, brzozowski and hello within noise (A alone varies 5% between rounds): no proven gain, reverted; the installBridge 7.4% is not the AsyncLocal write cost; next: allocation profile (gc-verbose) of term on lean_cic; 11:4x runtime knobs on the unchanged binary (ab-runtime*.ps1, 2 interleaved rounds, baseline noise about 0.3 s): the shipped config (server GC, concurrent, TieredPGO off) is already best: gen0 64 MB +10%, gen0 8 MB within noise, TieredCompilation off +15%, workstation GC +20-25% on lean_cic/spiral_proves (the hopac core allocates from several threads); GC tuning is ruled out; remaining levers: startup JIT (ReadyToRun, hello is 1.6 s of mostly startup) and algorithmic work in term; 11:4x gen0: test.ps1 sets DOTNET_GCgen0size=256 MB for every run; fresh-process probes (ab-gen0.ps1) show it 4-13% slower than the runtime default on lean_cic/spiral_proves in BOTH cores; but an A-B-A single-flight suite (aba-gen0-suite.ps1, warm workers, 236 C rows) shows no difference (summed 62.5 / 67.6 default / 67.4 s); test.ps1 left unchanged: switching it needs an A-B-A hopac -Suite all (fresh process per job) showing the gain; ReadyToRun is already applied by build.ps1 since 2026-10-05; 12:3x hopac harness default now warm-recycle with deferral (HOPAC-WARM-SERVER): suite 2.35x faster at identical rows", Epic, P1, D7, 35u32, Active, "", "compiler,hopac,performance", "current", "current")
inl portable_primitives () = Task ("PORTABLE-PRIMITIVES", "Replace C-only macros with portable ops: StringConcat, Floor/Ceil/Round/Atan2, string search/case, a char model, Zig/Lean/Bend arms in lib backend switches; 2026-10-08 13:1x lib/spiral math (edited in math.livemd via mix spiral.edit, math.spi re-exported and compared): floor/ceil/atan2/round gain C (__builtin_* with _Generic for f32/f64), Cpp (<cmath>), Delphi (Int/Frac/Ord, ArcTan2) and TypeScript arms; Lua and Gleam round fixed (gave 2 for 2.7 and 4 for 3.2; now the shared round_half_to_even); lib backend.spi dispatches C and Delphi (before: no lib function could reach a C arm); new sample portable_math_rounding: 10 backends, 9 native runs exit 0, all agree with the C oracle; 13:0x blessed the lib-using samples (30 rows; review and bless runs identical): portable_math_rounding new on 10 backends; format_any x2 C/Delphi now fail at the C/Pascal compiler with backend_switch_has_no_<backend>_arm_in_lib_spiral (BackendSwitch evaluates every arm, so a lib fallback cannot raise a Spiral error for one backend only, same as the Zig/Lean fallbacks); 7 F#/Rust/Zig rows changed only in variable numbering (proved by normalizing v<n>); next: console write_line/write for C and Delphi via the portable !!!!Printf with a typecase, which needs one agreed bool/float text across backends (F# True vs Rust true); 17:1x lib console (console.livemd via spiral.edit, console.spi re-exported): write_line/write gain C arms (printf via real typecase helpers write_line_c/write_c: string %s, i32, i64, u32, u64; floats and bools stay out: no shortest round-trip float text in C, F#/Python print True) and Delphi arms (Writeln/Write); TypeScript write_line moved from console.log to process.stdout.write(String(x)+newline): the harness runs TS in a Worker where console.log and process.stdout.write reorder, and console.log printed i64 BigInt as -7n; new sample portable_console_lines: 8 native backends, stdout identical to C; lib samples re-reviewed (zig_lib_console changed only in numbering); 19:5x lib convert (convert.livemd): convert_i32_base gains C (strtol) and Delphi (FPC radix prefixes ##36/##37/##38, base 2/8/10/16) arms; convert_i32 gains C/Delphi/TypeScript typed dispatch (string -> base 10, float -> round half even via nearbyint/Round, int -> cast); try_convert from string gains C/Delphi/TypeScript/Lua arms through parsed_integer (strict whole-text validation, never-throwing value expression, target range check via integer_fits) and Gleam trims like Rust; Lua previously returned the unparsed string, TypeScript had no convert_i32; lib console Gleam write_line/write print ints via int.to_string (io.println took only String); new sample portable_convert_parse: 7 native backends print 255/11/-42/123/none/none/7 like C; portable_console_lines now has a Gleam row", Feature, P1, D6, 60u32, Active, "", "compiler,lib,portability", "current", "current")
