inl c_user_globals_dropped () = Task ("C-USER-GLOBALS-DROPPED", "C backend drops every user global: CodegenC seeds its dedupe set from env.globals (global x = if has_added.Add x then globals.Add x) but prints only its private globals buffer, never env.globals, so !!!!Global / core global \"...\" text (e.g. #include) never reaches C output; the same in upstream The Spiral Language 2/CodegenC.fs (lines 175-176, 898); every other codegen prints env.globals; CodegenC maps to the upstream file, so the fix goes upstream (COMPILER-UPSTREAM-ONION) instead of a local edit; repro: tmp/cglobal (global \"#include <tgmath.h>\" absent from main.c); lib/spiral math C arms use __builtin_* with _Generic meanwhile; 13:4x FIXED here (correction: the upstream-section exception was only for comment stripping; functional fixes in CodegenC are the normal workflow, exported to the fork with scripts/upstream.py export --since): the C program assembly now writes env.globals before its own includes (Seq.append env.globals globals), as every other codegen does; repro tmp/cglobal now emits #include <tgmath.h>; upstream PR candidate (The Spiral Language 2/CodegenC.fs line 898)", TaskKind, P2, D2, 90u32, Active, "", "compiler,upstream,c", "current", "current")
inl ci_kino_shared_tmp_delete () = Task ("CI-KINO-SHARED-TMP-DELETE", "spiral ubuntu CI 18:34: 17 lib notebooks failed because spiral gleam/lua on CI delete their package dir = grandparent of the code file, which for Kino cells (/tmp/spiral_kino/<id>/main.gleam) is the shared /tmp/spiral_kino (other cells: could not write main.spi, remove_dir_all DirectoryNotEmpty); fix: package_owns_code (code under <package>/src) guards the CI deletion in process_gleam and process_lua; 21:1x verified locally with CI=1 and the Kino layout <root>/<id>/main.gleam plus a sibling <root>/other: unfixed CLI deleted the sibling and the root, fixed CLI keeps both (gleam.toml lands in the cell dir); apps/spiral rebuilt (run check: 43 notebook exports, rust/cuda ok) and shipped; first build failed because parsed_integer conv ran at peval for u = ref str via every BackendSwitch arm, now gated by a static integral check; 21:39 local CI=1 sweep with the fixed CLI: all 16 notebooks CI reported (sm, testing, guid, runtime, trace, resultm, base, date_time, math, optionm, listm, reflection, lustre, env, convert, console) exit 0 and %TEMP%/spiral_kino survives; parsing and file_system are the two known failures; awaits the next push", TaskKind, P0, D2, 90u32, Active, "", "ci,kino,spiral", "current", "current")
